MEF medium $\mathbf{(500ml)}$ To prepare $500\mathrm{ml}$ of MEF medium, in a tissue culture hood, supplement $447.5\mathrm{ml}$ of DMEM (high glucose, GlutaMAX supplement, pyruvate) with $50\mathrm{ml}$ of FBS and $2.5\mathrm{ml}$ of penicillin– streptomycin solution. MEF medium can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month. Human bFGF solution $(5~{\upmu}{\bf g}\ {\bf m}{\bf l}^{-1}$ )  In a tissue culture hood, reconstitute $100\upmu\mathrm{g}$ of human bFGF in $20~\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS with $0.2\%$ (wt/vol) sterile BSA. Divide the solution into aliquots and store them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 3 months.
Human ESC medium $\mathbf{500ml}$ )  To prepare $500~\mathrm{ml}$ of human ESC me­ dium, in a tissue culture hood, supplement $411.5~\mathrm{ml}$ of knockout DMEM with $75~\mathrm{ml}$ of KSR, $5~\mathrm{ml}$ of $\mathbf{L}$ -glutamine solution $\mathrm{\Omega}200\mathrm{mM},$ ), $5~\mathrm{ml}$ of nonessential amino acid solution $(100\times)$ , $2.5~\mathrm{ml}$ of penicillin–streptomy­ cin solution and $1\mathrm{ml}$ of $55~\mathrm{mM}$ $\upbeta$ -mercaptoethanol (final concentration $0.1~\mathrm{mM}$ ). Human ESC medium can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month. Freshly add human bFGF before use to a final concentration of $10~\mathrm{{ng}}$ $\mathrm{ml^{-1}}$ .  CRITICAL Keep human ESC medium protected from light, as KSR is light-sensitive.
Freezing medium $(50~\mathrm{ml})$ In a tissue culture hood, mix $18~\mathrm{ml}$ of DMEM, $27~\mathrm{ml}$ of FBS and $5\mathrm{ml}$ of DMSO. Freezing medium can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month.
Y-27632 stock solution $\mathbf{\dot{10}m M}$ )  In a tissue culture hood, dissolve $10~\mathrm{mg}$ of Y-27632 2HCl in $3.123~\mathrm{ml}$ of DMSO. Divide the solution into aliquots and store them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
Hypotonic solution  Dissolve $0.56\mathrm{g}$ of KCl and $0.5\mathrm{g}$ of sodium citrate in $200\mathrm{ml}$ of $\mathrm{dH}_{2}\mathrm{O}.$ . Hypotonic solution can be stored at room temperature for up to 1 year.
Fixative solution  In a chemical fume hood, mix $12~\mathrm{ml}$ of methanol with $4~\mathrm{ml}$ of acetic acid in a glass bottle. Fixative solution should be freshly prepared and kept at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ before use.
Buffer $\mathbf{pH6.8}$ Dissolve one tablet of buffer $\mathrm{pH}6.8$ in $1,000\mathrm{ml}$ of $\mathrm{dH}_{2}\mathrm{O}.$ Buffer $\mathrm{pH}6.8$ can be stored at $5{-}25^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and used up to the stated expiry date.
Hoechst 33342 stock solution (25 mg per ml)  In a tissue culture hood, dissolve $25\mathrm{mg}$ of Hoechst 33342 in $\mathrm{1ml}$ of sterile $\mathrm{\ddH}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ . Divide the solution into aliquots in light-protected microcentrifuge tubes, and store them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.  CRITICAL Keep Hoechst 33342 protected from light.
FACS medium  In a tissue culture hood, add $7.5\mathrm{ml}$ of KSR to $42.5\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS without $\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{MgCl}_{2}$ . FACS medium can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month. EQUIPMENT SETUP
Gelatin-coated plates  In a tissue culture hood, cover the bottom of the plates with $0.2\%$ (wt/vol) gelatin solution ( $1\mathrm{ml}$ per well of a six-well plate), and keep the plates at room temperature for $30\mathrm{min}$ . Aspirate the solution before use.
Matrigel-coated plates  Thaw Matrigel on ice. In a tissue culture hood, dilute Matrigel in cold $(4^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ DMEM/F12 at a ratio of 1:30 (vol/vol) and use the mixture to cover the bottom of the plates (for example, dilute $100\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of Matrigel in $3\mathrm{ml}$ of DMEM/F12, and cover the bottom of each well of a six-well plate with $0.5{\mathrm{ml}}$ of the mixture). Incubate the plates at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ , and aspirate the Matrigel-DMEM/F12 before use.  CRITICAL Matrigel solidifies at room temperature and should therefore be kept cold before coating. Glass microscope slides for metaphase spreading  In a chemical fume hood, submerge glass microscope slides in $100\%$ (vol/vol) ethanol at room temperature for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ . Dry the slides by gently wiping them with delicate task wipers on both sides. Write down sample information on the designated area of the slides, and put the slides into $\mathrm{dH}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ .
KSR-coated collection tubes  In a tissue culture hood, fill sterile $15\mathrm{-ml}$ coni­ cal tubes with FACS medium (prepared as described in the Reagent Setup) and store them at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for at least $^{\textrm{1h}}$ before FACS. Before use, aspirate the medium and replace it with $\mathrm{1-2~ml}$ of human ESC medium containing 10 $\upmu\mathrm{M}$ Y-27632 (Y-27632 stock solution diluted 1:1,000).
