(vii) Plate the human ESCs on the MEF-containing plates by transferring $2~\mathsf{m l}$ of the cell suspension to each well of the six-well plates, and place the plates in the incubator. To disperse the cells evenly, gently, yet quickly, rock the plates back and forth and sideways a few times. iii) On the next day and onward, change the medium daily using fresh, warm $(37^{\circ}\mathsf{C})$ human ESC medium. $\blacktriangle$ CRITICAL STEP It is important to monitor the cells daily under the microscope to assess their growth rate.   
