(viii) Repeat Step 2A(vii) at least twice more using $2~\mathsf{m l}$ of fixative solution. Centrifuge the cells at $150g$ for 5 min at room temperature, aspirate the supernatant, and resuspend the cell pellet in $1.5~\mathsf{m l}$ of fixative solution as in Step 2A(vi). Keep the sample at $-20\ ^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ overnight or longer.  PAUSE POINT Fixed samples can be stored at $-20\ ^{\circ}\ C$ for several months.   
